oenix Contact ... NS-35-7.5 ... ~ £113.20\"; Page 43: \"Braze Ring Fitting ... Harris ... Stay-Silv-15 ... Unit ~ £17.24 ... Line £206.88\"; Page 49: \"LCD Thermostat Panel ... Siemens ... RDS-110 ... ~ £0.14\".\n        *   Root cause in chain: Engine B (`engine_b_prices.ts`) failed to retrieve real-world prices and fell back to a static array of arbitrary price anchors (e.g., £113.20, £17.24, £2.96, £0.14) which it mapped randomly to components without any class-based sanity checking or parametric scaling.\n        *   ","refusal":null,"reasoning":"**Reviewing ASHP Report**\n\nI'm currently performing a rigorous, highly technical engineering critique of an AI-generated PDF report concerning an 8 kW residential Air-Source Heat Pump utilizing R290. My focus is on validating its technical accuracy and adherence to engineering principles.\n\n**Analyzing ASHP Report Details**\n\nI'm deep into dissecting this ASHP report, scrutinizing it against a precise set of engineering criteria. My aim is to uncover any technical discrepancies or omissions within its physics, regulatory compliance, and Bill of Materials realism, ensuring the AI's output meets the exacting standards expected by industry veterans.\n\n**Validating Report Logic**\n\nI'm currently cross-referencing the AI's cost estimations, specifically the Bill of Materials and manufacturing figures, against its stated installed pricing. I'm investigating potential inconsistencies between the cover page figures and the detailed BoM to ensure internal coherence and realism in its economic projections.\n\n**Identifying BoM Discrepancy**\n\nI've identified a significant inconsistency. The report discusses 30 kW units and their economies of scale, which directly contradicts the 8 kW residential ASHP brief. This appears to be a synthesis error, pulling in reference data for a larger system. I've flagged this for cost calibration.\n\n**Checking Compressor Specs**\n\nI am currently examining the compressor's electrical input